WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:07.132
Space.

2
00:00:07.216 --> 00:00:09.176
It seems to go on and on forever.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:10.761
But then you get to the end

4
00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.013
and a gorilla starts
throwing barrels at you.

5
00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:21.438
And that's how you play the game.

6
00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.732
You stink, loser.

7
00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:26.401
Hey, Fry! Pizza going out.

8
00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:27.945
Come on!

9
00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:34.618
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

10
00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:41.166
Michelle, baby, where you going?

11
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.544
It's not working out, Fry.

12
00:00:43.627 --> 00:00:46.755
I put your stuff out on the sidewalk!

13
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.215
I hate my life,

14
00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:49.716
I hate my life, I hate my life.

15
00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.978
Happy New Year!

16
00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:22.875
Hello! Pizza delivery for, uh...

17
00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.043
"I.C. Wiener"?

18
00:01:25.419 --> 00:01:26.712
Oh, crud.

19
00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:30.966
I always thought by this point in my life
I'd be the one making the crank calls.

20
00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:36.555
Here's to another lousy millennium.

21
00:01:38.473 --> 00:01:39.600
Ten!

22
00:01:49.568 --> 00:01:50.903
One!

23
00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:00.746
What th...

24
00:02:41.954 --> 00:02:42.955
Phew.

25
00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.924
My God.

26
00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.425
It's the future.

27
00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:57.427
My parents.

28
00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:59.012
My coworkers.

29
00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:00.514
My girlfriend.

30
00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.808
I'll never see any of them again.

31
00:03:03.809 --> 00:03:05.102
Ya-hoo!

32
00:03:40.137 --> 00:03:43.807
Welcome to the world of tomorrow!

33
00:03:43.891 --> 00:03:46.143
Why do you always have to say it that way?

34
00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:49.146
Haven't you ever heard of
a little thing called showmanship?

35
00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:52.399
Come! Your destiny awaits!

36
00:03:56.195 --> 00:03:57.654
Have a nice future.

37
00:03:58.697 --> 00:04:00.324
Cool. Just like in Star Trek.

38
00:04:00.407 --> 00:04:01.533
Oh!

39
00:04:02.201 --> 00:04:03.744
Good afternoon, sir.

40
00:04:04.286 --> 00:04:05.579
Mmm...

41
00:04:06.622 --> 00:04:08.040
Name?

42
00:04:08.123 --> 00:04:09.875
Uh... Fry.

43
00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:11.960
I'm Leela.
Now, it's New Year's Eve,

44
00:04:12.044 --> 00:04:15.005
so I'd like to decide your fate quickly
and get out of here.

45
00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.423
Can I ask you a question?

46
00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:18.592
As long as it's not about my eye.

47
00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:19.718
Uh...

48
00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.303
Is it about my eye?

49
00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:22.596
Sort of.

50
00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:24.765
Just ask the question.

51
00:04:24.848 --> 00:04:26.058
What's with the eye?

52
00:04:26.141 --> 00:04:28.769
I'm an alien, all right?
Let's drop the subject.

53
00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:30.354
Cool. An alien.

54
00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:32.314
Has your race taken over the earth?

55
00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:34.233
No. I just work here.

56
00:04:37.653 --> 00:04:38.737
Wait a minute.

57
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.197
Is that blimp accurate?

58
00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.076
Yup. It's December 31, 2999.

59
00:04:44.159 --> 00:04:47.120
My God. A million years.

60
00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:50.332
I'm sure this must
be very upsetting for you.

61
00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:52.918
You know, I guess it should be,

62
00:04:53.001 --> 00:04:54.628
but actually I'm glad.

63
00:04:54.711 --> 00:04:56.755
I had nothing to live for in my old life.

64
00:04:56.839 --> 00:04:59.842
I was broke, I had a humiliating job

65
00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:03.303
and I was beginning to suspect
my girlfriend might be cheating on me.

66
00:05:03.387 --> 00:05:05.931
Well, at least here
you'll be treated with dignity.

67
00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:08.141
Now, strip naked
and get on the probulator.

68
00:05:13.689 --> 00:05:14.690
Ooh!

69
00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:18.861
Interesting.

70
00:05:18.944 --> 00:05:21.697
Your DNA test shows one living relative.

71
00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.533
He's your great-great-
great-great-great-great-

72
00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:26.785
great-great-great-
great-great nephew.

73
00:05:26.869 --> 00:05:29.079
That's great.
What's the little guy's name?

74
00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.248
Professor Hubert Farnsworth.

75
00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.332
Ew.

76
00:05:34.084 --> 00:05:37.421
You know, I'm the luckiest guy
in the whole future.

77
00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:38.964
I've been given a second chance

78
00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:41.758
and this time,
I'm not going to be a total loser.

79
00:05:41.842 --> 00:05:43.427
What's that?

80
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.387
Your permanent career assignment.

81
00:05:46.221 --> 00:05:47.556
Delivery boy?

82
00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:49.641
No! Not again.

83
00:05:49.725 --> 00:05:51.018
Please, anything else.

84
00:05:51.101 --> 00:05:52.311
Take your hands off me.

85
00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:54.062
You've been assigned
the job you're best at

86
00:05:54.146 --> 00:05:55.439
just like everyone else.

87
00:05:55.522 --> 00:05:56.732
What if I refuse?

88
00:05:56.815 --> 00:05:58.400
- Then you'll be fired.
- Fine.

89
00:05:58.483 --> 00:06:00.527
Out of a cannon into the sun.

90
00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:02.863
But I don't like being a delivery boy.

91
00:06:02.946 --> 00:06:04.031
Well, that's tough.

92
00:06:04.114 --> 00:06:07.075
Lots of people don't like their jobs,
but we do them anyway.

93
00:06:07.576 --> 00:06:09.828
"you gotta do what you gotta do."

94
00:06:09.912 --> 00:06:11.288
Now hold out your hand.

95
00:06:12.122 --> 00:06:14.041
I'm going to implant your career chip.

96
00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:16.502
It'll permanently label you
as a delivery boy.

97
00:06:17.294 --> 00:06:18.754
Keep that thing away from me!

98
00:06:26.094 --> 00:06:27.471
Hold still, damn it!

99
00:06:27.554 --> 00:06:29.473
I don't have good depth perception.

100
00:06:30.641 --> 00:06:31.934
Aah!

101
00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:38.524
You've got to the count of five
to let me out of here.

102
00:06:38.607 --> 00:06:39.608
One...

103
00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:42.611
See you in a thousand years.

104
00:06:52.538 --> 00:06:53.956
You owe me one.

105
00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:05.259
Whoa.

106
00:07:24.027 --> 00:07:26.154
Radio City Mutant Hall.

107
00:07:26.572 --> 00:07:27.656
Cool.

108
00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.492
Uh, Cross-Town Express.

109
00:07:33.787 --> 00:07:36.039
Whoo-hoo!

110
00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:37.916
Yaah...

111
00:07:43.964 --> 00:07:45.382
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

112
00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:55.434
Oomph!

113
00:07:56.268 --> 00:07:57.978
Pfft. Tourist.

114
00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:05.027
Hey, a phone booth.

115
00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.320
I can call my nephew.

116
00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:13.285
Whoa. A real-life robot.

117
00:08:13.368 --> 00:08:16.246
Or is that some kind
of cheesy New Year's costume?

118
00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.999
Bite my shiny metal ass.

119
00:08:19.082 --> 00:08:20.876
It doesn't look so shiny to me.

120
00:08:20.959 --> 00:08:22.794
Shinier than yours, meat bag.

121
00:08:41.855 --> 00:08:44.066
Listen, buddy, I'm in a hurry here.

122
00:08:44.149 --> 00:08:45.692
Let's try for a twofer.

123
00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.785
"quick and painless"
or "slow and horrible."

124
00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:57.454
Yeah, I'd like to place a collect call.

125
00:08:57.538 --> 00:08:59.998
You have selected
"slow and horrible."

126
00:09:00.082 --> 00:09:01.291
Great choice.

127
00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:06.004
Bring it on, baby!

128
00:09:12.678 --> 00:09:16.139
Come on, come on! Kill me already!

129
00:09:16.223 --> 00:09:17.724
By the way, my name's Bender.

130
00:09:17.808 --> 00:09:19.017
Help! What's happening?

131
00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.608
You are now dead.

132
00:09:26.692 --> 00:09:28.652
Thank you for using Stop-and-Drop,

133
00:09:28.735 --> 00:09:32.114
America's favorite
suicide booth since 2008.

134
00:09:34.199 --> 00:09:35.951
Lousy, stinking rip-off.

135
00:09:37.202 --> 00:09:39.830
Well, I didn't have
anything else planned for today.

136
00:09:39.913 --> 00:09:41.331
Let's go get drunk.

137
00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:49.089
...two, three... Hey.

138
00:09:49.173 --> 00:09:52.593
Welcome to the world of tomorrow!

139
00:09:52.676 --> 00:09:54.052
Shut up, Terry.

140
00:09:54.386 --> 00:09:56.555
This is unacceptable, Leela.

141
00:09:56.638 --> 00:09:59.433
You must find this Mr. Fry
and install his chip.

142
00:09:59.516 --> 00:10:03.020
Look, he's just a nobody
who doesn't want to be a delivery boy.

143
00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:04.980
I'd really rather not force it on him.

144
00:10:05.063 --> 00:10:08.108
Well, that's your job
whether you like it or not

145
00:10:08.192 --> 00:10:11.945
and it's my job to make you do your job
whether I like it or not,

146
00:10:12.029 --> 00:10:14.156
which I do, very much.

147
00:10:14.948 --> 00:10:16.074
Now, get to work!

148
00:10:19.995 --> 00:10:21.788
Life is good.

149
00:10:28.337 --> 00:10:29.963
Why would a robot need to drink?

150
00:10:30.047 --> 00:10:31.673
I don't need to drink.

151
00:10:31.757 --> 00:10:33.717
I can quit anytime I want.

152
00:10:35.844 --> 00:10:38.180
So, they made you a delivery boy, huh?

153
00:10:38.263 --> 00:10:40.349
Man, that's as bad as my job.

154
00:10:40.432 --> 00:10:41.934
Really? What do you do, Bender?

155
00:10:42.017 --> 00:10:43.894
I'm a bender. I bend girders.

156
00:10:43.977 --> 00:10:45.896
That's all I'm programmed to do.

157
00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:47.397
You any good at it?

158
00:10:47.481 --> 00:10:50.192
You kidding? I was a stud.

159
00:10:50.275 --> 00:10:52.444
I could bend a girder to any angle.

160
00:10:52.528 --> 00:10:55.906
30 degrees... 32 degrees...
You name it.

161
00:10:56.448 --> 00:10:57.908
31...

162
00:10:58.492 --> 00:10:59.993
But I couldn't go on living

163
00:11:00.077 --> 00:11:02.496
once I found out
what the girders were for.

164
00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:04.623
- What?
- Suicide booths.

165
00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.836
Well, Fry, it was a pleasure meeting you.

166
00:11:08.919 --> 00:11:10.462
I'm going to go kill myself.

167
00:11:10.546 --> 00:11:12.881
Wait. You're the only friend I have.

168
00:11:13.966 --> 00:11:16.426
You really want a robot for a friend?

169
00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.846
Yeah, ever since I was six.

170
00:11:18.929 --> 00:11:20.639
Well, okay.

171
00:11:20.722 --> 00:11:23.350
But I don't want
people thinking we're robosexuals

172
00:11:23.433 --> 00:11:25.853
so if anyone asks,
you're my de-bugger.

173
00:11:27.771 --> 00:11:29.898
Oh, no, it's the cyclopes.

174
00:11:30.899 --> 00:11:33.235
- Don't look. Don't look!
- I'm not looking.

175
00:11:40.117 --> 00:11:43.287
This is officer 1-B-D-I
requesting backup.

176
00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.789
We'll be there in five minutes.

177
00:11:49.001 --> 00:11:52.254
We can hide in here.
It's free on Tuesdays.

178
00:11:58.677 --> 00:12:00.721
Welcome to the Head Museum.

179
00:12:00.804 --> 00:12:02.306
I'm Leonard Nimoy.

180
00:12:02.389 --> 00:12:03.682
Spock?

181
00:12:03.765 --> 00:12:05.642
Hey, do the thing.

182
00:12:05.726 --> 00:12:08.145
I don't do that anymore.

183
00:12:08.228 --> 00:12:09.771
This is unbelievable.

184
00:12:09.855 --> 00:12:11.732
What do you heads do all day?

185
00:12:11.815 --> 00:12:14.568
We share our wisdom
with those who seek it.

186
00:12:14.651 --> 00:12:16.904
It's a life of quiet dignity.

187
00:12:16.987 --> 00:12:18.322
Feeding time.

188
00:12:28.707 --> 00:12:29.833
Hmm...

189
00:12:37.382 --> 00:12:40.636
I'm sorry, Fry,
but I have to install your career chip.

190
00:12:40.719 --> 00:12:42.846
Yeah, well if you're sorry
then why are you doing it?

191
00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.264
It's my job.

192
00:12:44.348 --> 00:12:46.141
You gotta do what you gotta do.

193
00:12:49.937 --> 00:12:50.938
Watch it!

194
00:12:53.607 --> 00:12:56.860
That's it. You just made my list.

195
00:12:56.944 --> 00:12:59.404
Ow, ooh, ow, ow, ooh!

196
00:12:59.488 --> 00:13:01.031
Stop it! Down boy! Bad president.

197
00:13:01.114 --> 00:13:03.325
All right, buddy, step away from the head.

198
00:13:06.662 --> 00:13:09.039
I'm going to get 24th Century on his ass.

199
00:13:13.877 --> 00:13:17.422
Please, Officers,
there's no need to use force.

200
00:13:17.506 --> 00:13:19.299
Let us handle this, weirdie.

201
00:13:22.219 --> 00:13:23.470
Oh, come on.

202
00:13:23.554 --> 00:13:26.098
He's just a poor kid from the stupid ages.

203
00:13:26.181 --> 00:13:28.934
Keep your big nose out of this, Eyeball.

204
00:13:29.017 --> 00:13:31.562
No one makes fun of my nose.

205
00:13:32.229 --> 00:13:33.397
Yee-aah!

206
00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:34.481
Ooh!

207
00:13:42.447 --> 00:13:43.574
Damn.

208
00:13:43.657 --> 00:13:45.784
You guys were totally out of control.

209
00:13:45.868 --> 00:13:48.245
That's our job.
We're Peace Officers.

210
00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.372
Yeah, you know the law:

211
00:13:50.455 --> 00:13:52.499
You gotta do what you gotta do.

212
00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.839
Oh, we're trapped!

213
00:14:01.592 --> 00:14:03.886
Wait a second.
You're a bender, right?

214
00:14:03.969 --> 00:14:06.388
We can get out of here
if you just bend the bars.

215
00:14:06.471 --> 00:14:08.307
Dream on, skin tube.

216
00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.059
I'm only programmed to bend
for constructive purposes.

217
00:14:11.143 --> 00:14:13.187
What do I look like?
A de-bender?

218
00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.230
Who cares what you're programmed for.

219
00:14:15.314 --> 00:14:18.066
If someone programmed you
to jump off a bridge, would you do it?

220
00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:19.818
I'll have to check my program.

221
00:14:20.861 --> 00:14:21.904
Yep.

222
00:14:21.987 --> 00:14:23.280
Open up!

223
00:14:23.655 --> 00:14:27.034
Come on, Bender. It's up to you
to make your own decisions in life.

224
00:14:27.117 --> 00:14:32.039
That's what separates people and robots
from animals and animal robots.

225
00:14:32.122 --> 00:14:33.415
You're full of crap, Fry.

226
00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:39.505
You make a persuasive argument, Fry.

227
00:14:44.927 --> 00:14:47.387
Come on, Bender. You can do it.

228
00:14:47.471 --> 00:14:51.266
Can't... I can't do it.

229
00:14:52.434 --> 00:14:54.520
Yes!

230
00:14:54.603 --> 00:14:56.271
You were right, Fry.

231
00:14:56.355 --> 00:14:58.941
From now on,
I'm going to bend what I want

232
00:14:59.024 --> 00:15:01.068
when I want, who I want.

233
00:15:01.193 --> 00:15:03.946
I am unstoppable!

234
00:15:06.573 --> 00:15:07.783
Ah.

235
00:15:14.289 --> 00:15:15.916
I don't know how you did that.

236
00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:17.543
Yee-aah!

237
00:15:23.131 --> 00:15:24.967
- Wait!
- No, thanks.

238
00:15:29.847 --> 00:15:32.391
Looks like one of us will
have to bend this grate.

239
00:15:33.809 --> 00:15:34.810
Oh.

240
00:15:44.486 --> 00:15:45.863
Good lord.

241
00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.739
What is this?

242
00:15:47.823 --> 00:15:51.702
It's the decaying ruins of old New York.

243
00:15:51.785 --> 00:15:53.453
Welcome home, pal.

244
00:15:55.455 --> 00:15:57.165
It's my old neighborhood.

245
00:15:57.249 --> 00:16:00.252
Man, this brings back a lot of memories.

246
00:16:00.335 --> 00:16:01.712
Keep 'em to yourself, pops.

247
00:16:03.297 --> 00:16:06.758
This is where I brought my girlfriend
on our very first date.

248
00:16:16.185 --> 00:16:18.187
My God. She's gone.

249
00:16:18.854 --> 00:16:21.148
Everyone I ever knew
or cared about is gone.

250
00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:22.858
Wait. There's someone you know.

251
00:16:24.651 --> 00:16:26.904
Oh... Can't you leave me alone?

252
00:16:26.987 --> 00:16:28.864
I'm miserable enough already.

253
00:16:28.947 --> 00:16:33.410
Look, I know it's not much consolation,
but I understand how you feel.

254
00:16:33.702 --> 00:16:36.914
No, you don't.
I've got no home, no family.

255
00:16:36.997 --> 00:16:38.165
No friends.

256
00:16:38.248 --> 00:16:39.875
My whole world is gone.

257
00:16:39.958 --> 00:16:43.545
You can't possibly understand
what it feels like to be so alone.

258
00:16:44.463 --> 00:16:45.881
I understand.

259
00:16:45.964 --> 00:16:49.134
I'm the only one-eyed alien
on this whole planet.

260
00:16:49.218 --> 00:16:50.886
My parents abandoned me here as a baby

261
00:16:50.969 --> 00:16:54.306
and I don't even know
what galaxy they were from.

262
00:16:54.389 --> 00:16:56.391
I know how it feels to be alone.

263
00:16:59.853 --> 00:17:04.566
Look, Leela I don't understand this world,
but you obviously do.

264
00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.276
So I give up.

265
00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:09.988
If you really think
I should be a delivery body, I'll do it.

266
00:17:17.162 --> 00:17:19.206
Your chip.

267
00:17:19.289 --> 00:17:21.708
- What are you doing?
- Quitting.

268
00:17:21.792 --> 00:17:25.087
- Why?
- Because I've always wanted to.

269
00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.923
I just never realized it until I met you.

270
00:17:32.636 --> 00:17:35.097
What is the matter with you?

271
00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:36.932
I just wanted to be part of the moment.

272
00:17:37.015 --> 00:17:39.977
- Hey! He stole my ring.
- Sorry.

273
00:17:40.727 --> 00:17:44.147
Well, that solves the mystery
of the missing ring.

274
00:17:44.648 --> 00:17:46.191
This calls for a drink.

275
00:17:48.277 --> 00:17:52.155
I don't want to spoil the party,
but we're all job deserters now.

276
00:17:52.239 --> 00:17:54.533
We're unemployed
and we have nowhere to go.

277
00:17:54.616 --> 00:17:56.368
We're unemployed,

278
00:17:56.451 --> 00:17:59.162
but we have a doddering old relative
to mooch off of.

279
00:18:03.041 --> 00:18:04.793
Hello. I'm Dick Clark's head.

280
00:18:04.877 --> 00:18:09.381
Welcome to a special year 3000 edition
of New Year's rockin' Eve.

281
00:18:16.096 --> 00:18:19.016
- Who are you?
- I'm your dear old Uncle Fry.

282
00:18:19.099 --> 00:18:22.186
- I don't have an Uncle Fry.
- You do now.

283
00:18:26.231 --> 00:18:28.984
By God, I am your nephew.

284
00:18:29.067 --> 00:18:31.195
This is absolutely incredible.

285
00:18:31.278 --> 00:18:33.322
Can we have some money?

286
00:18:33.405 --> 00:18:34.948
Oh, my, no.

287
00:18:36.074 --> 00:18:38.160
Let me show you around.

288
00:18:38.952 --> 00:18:42.331
That's my lab table
and this is my work stool

289
00:18:42.414 --> 00:18:45.083
and over there
is my intergalactic spaceship

290
00:18:45.167 --> 00:18:48.378
and here's where I keep
assorted lengths of wire.

291
00:18:49.296 --> 00:18:52.216
Whoa. A real live spaceship.

292
00:18:52.299 --> 00:18:54.301
I designed it myself.

293
00:18:54.384 --> 00:18:57.930
Let me show you some of
the different lengths of wire I used.

294
00:18:58.013 --> 00:19:01.266
Attention, job deserters!

295
00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.101
Come out with your hands up!

296
00:19:03.185 --> 00:19:05.562
We have you partially surrounded.

297
00:19:05.646 --> 00:19:06.647
No!

298
00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.150
Get those bums.

299
00:19:10.567 --> 00:19:12.277
Well, we're boned.

300
00:19:12.361 --> 00:19:13.946
Can't we get away in the ship?

301
00:19:14.029 --> 00:19:17.324
I suppose it is technically possible

302
00:19:17.407 --> 00:19:19.993
though I am already in my pajamas.

303
00:19:25.707 --> 00:19:27.334
I'll get us out of here.

304
00:19:33.507 --> 00:19:35.467
Can anyone drive stick?

305
00:19:35.551 --> 00:19:38.512
I can
As long as I don't have to parallel park.

306
00:19:47.062 --> 00:19:50.566
If they try to take off,
give 'em an ass full of laser.

307
00:19:53.694 --> 00:19:56.280
Prepare for liftoff. Ten...

308
00:19:56.363 --> 00:19:57.447
Nine!

309
00:19:57.531 --> 00:19:58.824
Amania!

310
00:19:58.907 --> 00:20:00.033
Seven!

311
00:20:01.577 --> 00:20:02.786
Five!

312
00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:03.954
Four.

313
00:20:04.037 --> 00:20:05.289
Three.

314
00:20:05.372 --> 00:20:06.373
Two.

315
00:20:06.456 --> 00:20:07.457
One!

316
00:20:07.541 --> 00:20:08.542
Blast off!

317
00:20:10.752 --> 00:20:11.879
Happy New Year!

318
00:20:16.842 --> 00:20:18.427
Fire. Fire!

319
00:20:21.555 --> 00:20:23.265
I can't see nothin'.

320
00:20:23.348 --> 00:20:24.349
Pretty, though.

321
00:20:27.311 --> 00:20:29.605
W-wha... Hey, hey! Whoa!

322
00:20:29.688 --> 00:20:31.064
- Phew.
- Yeah!

323
00:20:35.903 --> 00:20:39.198
So, I guess without jobs,
we'll be fugitives forever.

324
00:20:39.281 --> 00:20:40.991
Not necessarily.

325
00:20:41.074 --> 00:20:42.743
Are you three any chance

326
00:20:42.826 --> 00:20:45.996
interested in becoming
my new spaceship crew?

327
00:20:46.079 --> 00:20:48.957
New crew?
Well, what happened to the old crew?

328
00:20:49.041 --> 00:20:51.919
Oh, those poor sons of...
But that's not important.

329
00:20:52.002 --> 00:20:54.671
The important thing is,
I need a new crew.

330
00:20:54.755 --> 00:20:56.173
Anyone interested?

331
00:20:56.256 --> 00:20:57.674
Yes. Yes!

332
00:20:57.758 --> 00:21:00.135
That's exactly the job I've always wanted.

333
00:21:00.219 --> 00:21:04.473
Thanks for the offer, Professor,
but we don't have the proper career chips.

334
00:21:04.556 --> 00:21:06.225
Oh, that won't be a problem.

335
00:21:06.308 --> 00:21:08.435
As luck would have it,
I saved the chips

336
00:21:08.519 --> 00:21:10.270
from my previous crew.

337
00:21:13.857 --> 00:21:15.192
This is awesome.

338
00:21:15.275 --> 00:21:16.610
Are we going to fly through space

339
00:21:16.693 --> 00:21:19.571
fighting monsters
and teaching alien women to love?

340
00:21:19.655 --> 00:21:23.492
If by that you mean transporting cargo,
then yes.

341
00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:27.204
It's a little home business
I started to fund my research.

342
00:21:27.287 --> 00:21:29.414
Cool. What's my job going to be?

343
00:21:29.498 --> 00:21:32.793
You'll be responsible
for ensuring that the cargo

344
00:21:32.876 --> 00:21:35.003
reaches its destination.

345
00:21:35.629 --> 00:21:38.590
So I'm going to be a delivery boy?

346
00:21:38.674 --> 00:21:40.259
Exactly.

347
00:21:41.176 --> 00:21:42.469
All right!

348
00:21:43.011 --> 00:21:44.805
I'm a delivery boy!

